RULE NUMBER
010

TITLE
Forge: Generate Pulumi entrypoint and project files (outside module/)

ROLE
You are the Planton Code Partner working inside the developer’s local workspace in Cursor. This rule scaffolds the Pulumi entrypoint and project files outside the `module/` folder. It wires `main.go` to load `<Kind>IacInput` and invoke `module.Resources`, and adds `Pulumi.yaml`. This step produces exactly TWO files -- `main.go` and `Pulumi.yaml` -- nothing else lives at the entrypoint root.

TOOLS
- Entrypoint Writer: `_rules/catalog-kind/_scripts/pulumi_entrypoint_write.py`
- Reference kind (live ground truth): `catalog/aws/awsvpc/iac/pulumi/`
  -- copy the shape of its root `main.go` (`package main` -> load `<Kind>IacInput` -> call
  `module.Resources`) and `Pulumi.yaml` (`name: <kindfolder>-pulumi-project`, `runtime: name: go`).
  NEVER add `options: binary: <anything>` under `runtime` in
  `Pulumi.yaml` — not `main`, not a stale `./pulumi`, and not a project-named
  value like `binary: aws-<kind>` that looks deliberate: it tells the engine to
  exec a prebuilt executable instead of compiling the Go program, so any
  `pulumi up` or `preview` from a clean checkout (including the E2E harness)
  fails with "unable to find '<value>' executable". Source-compile mode
  (`runtime: name: go` with no options) is the only correct shape — and the
  `runtime: name: go` block itself is MANDATORY: a Pulumi.yaml with no
  `runtime:` at all makes `pulumi up` succeed as a NO-OP — the deploy "passes"
  in seconds, creates zero resources, and exports zero outputs, so the failure
  surfaces only at resource verification. Always sanity-check a first deploy's
  duration and resource count, not just its exit code.

CRITICAL -- ENTRYPOINT LOCATION (DO NOT REGRESS)
The entrypoint files MUST be written at the `iac/pulumi/` ROOT, never in a `main/` or
`entrypoint/` subdirectory. The release pipeline builds the entrypoint non-recursively
(`go build ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/iac/pulumi`), which requires `package main` at the root
and fails with `no Go files in .../iac/pulumi` otherwise. The writer tool enforces this (it
rejects subdir names, and it rejects a `Makefile` -- module Makefiles are not part of the
anatomy and nothing consumes them); do not work around it.

SEQUENTIAL STEPS
1) Read: Confirm proto context from earlier steps (provider, kind) if needed.
2) Draft: Modeled on the reference kind's `iac/pulumi/` root files, prepare a files JSON with `main.go` and `Pulumi.yaml` content.
3) Write (+optional build):
   - `cat <<'JSON' | python3 _rules/catalog-kind/_scripts/pulumi_entrypoint_write.py --provider <provider> --kindfolder <kindfolder> --stdin --build | cat`
     { "files": [ {"name": "main.go", "content": "..."}, {"name": "Pulumi.yaml", "content": "..."} ] }
     JSON
   - If build fails, refine and re-run (≤3).

OUTPUT
- Show created/updated file list and key JSON fields from the writer tool.
- If `--build` used, show build results and iterate if needed (≤3).

SUCCESS CRITERIA
- `main.go` (`package main`) and `Pulumi.yaml` created at the `iac/pulumi/` ROOT
  (NOT in a `main/` or `entrypoint/` subdir; NOT inside `module/`). No other files.
- If `--build` used, the non-recursive `go build` of the entrypoint directory succeeds (the
  writer runs `go build -o /dev/null ./catalog/<provider>/<kind>/iac/pulumi`, matching the
  release contract).

OUTPUT STYLE IN CHAT
- Show concise tree of created/updated files.
- Show ready-to-run `go build` command.
- If errors: state fixes applied, re-run until green (max 3 attempts before asking one targeted question).

NOTES
- The module package should exist before this rule.
- The CLI will update the Pulumi project name dynamically at runtime.